You make a good point. String concatenation in Python can be costly in terms of time and space complexity, particularly within loops. Using a list to store characters can be an optimized approach. This is because lists in Python are mutable and have O(1) time complexity for append operations, which is much faster compared to concatenating immutable strings. Here is the modified version of the code which utilizes a list for storing character sequence.

